hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1398","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The sun eclipsed on The time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he led the people in prayer, mentioned the hadith, and said at the end of it: Then he left and said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon will not be eclipsed.” For the death of anyone, nor for his life, but they are two signs of God, so if you see that, then hurry to prayer.” This is what Al-Zuhri said. He said: Hisham added to it: “If you see that, give alms and pray.”"
"1399","Abu Al-Azhar narrated to us, and I wrote it down from its origin. He said: Yunus narrated to us, meaning Ibn Muhammad Al-Mu’addib, Falayh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abbad. Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Asmaa bint Abi Bakr, that she said: The sun was eclipsed at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: “So when you see that, rush to prayer, to the remembrance of God, and to charity.”"
"1400","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the sun was eclipsed on the day Abraham, the son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so the people thought it was eclipsed. Because of his death, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and said: “O people, the sun and the moon are two signs of God. They are not eclipsed due to the death of anyone or For his life, so when you see that, proceed to prayer and to the remembrance of God, and supplicate and give alms.”"
